      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start, it definitely feels more premium than my last draft. However, the prestige auditor just flagged this one with a pretty mediocre score—it's saying the \"luxury density\" is too low for a property of this caliber. \n\nI know I said not to spam it, but the marketing director is really pushing for that \"ultra-luxury\" feel to justify the price tag. Can you try a second version? Try to weave in more of those high-end, evocative terms to bring that score up, but please, for the love of god, make sure the actual specs (the 4 bedrooms and the 8500 sq ft) are still very easy to find and read. I don't want the client thinking we're hiding the details behind a wall of flowery words, we just need it to hit harder.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
